  occurring  now those collectively i'm going to do  leads me to my second phase  all right which is the monitoring  and in the monitoring phase i'm going to  take all these actions that i have and  my goal here is to really make my  find out how do i digitally represent  this process that i'm actually going  through now this is the actual into  invisibility of what's actually  occurring so a lot of times one of the  benefits of process mining why it is  important is because you actually get to  associate actions to a particular  workflow some of those are happy paths  and some of those can be those ones that  take you out in the left field that you  spend a lot of time doing but the most  important thing is that you get to  actually physically represent this along  with metrics that go along with it to  know  the next step is the optimization  now in this step in this phase rather  i'll have the visibility of having a  self  service dashboard  and it will give me the ability to  oversee this process get particular  metrics that i can really start to  understand how am i performing all right  another great benefit of this is this is  really where you start to bring in can  really take on the early beginnings the  foundations of automation  what they like to call intelligent  automation where i can use many  different types of technology to look at  this process that i have this path and  how can i make each one of those  efficient now if you are coming to this  brand new process mining is your path to  know where to start first  naturally just having a process that you  are going through it may be a little  difficult it will be difficult to know  where to start from this gives you an  entry point  and metrics to know when i am getting  something making it very efficient and  the fact that i have access that i'm  using with  my it systems along with the actual raw  data of every task that everybody is  doing everyone does in this workflow it  really gives me the not 